Q2. Why does Rectangle-Square violate LSP?

Interview Ready Answer

Suppose

Rectangle allows

Width = 5

Height = 10

Area = 50

------------------------------------------------------------

Now,

Square extends Rectangle.

Square forces

Width = Height

Client Code

Rectangle r = new Square();

r.setWidth(5);

r.setHeight(10);

Expected

Area = 50

Actual

Width = 10

Height = 10

Area = 100

The program behavior changes after replacing
Rectangle with Square.

Therefore,

Square cannot safely replace Rectangle.

LSP is violated.

