Q3. How should Rectangle and Square be designed
to follow LSP?

Interview Ready Answer

Wrong Design

Rectangle

    ▲

    │

Square

Square changes the expected behavior
of Rectangle.

Therefore,

LSP is violated.

------------------------------------------------------------

Correct Design

              Shape

             /     \

            /       \

     Rectangle     Square

Both implement the same abstraction.

Neither inherits from the other.

Example

interface Shape{

    int getArea();
}

------------------------------------------------------------

class Rectangle implements Shape{

    private int length;

    private int breadth;

    public int getArea(){

        return length*breadth;
    }
}

------------------------------------------------------------

class Square implements Shape{

    private int side;

    public int getArea(){

        return side*side;
    }
}

Both classes have independent behavior.

LSP is satisfied.

