Q4. Difference between Inheritance and LSP

Interview Ready Answer

Inheritance

• Used for Code Reuse.
• Establishes an IS-A relationship.
• Child inherits parent's properties and methods.
• Does NOT guarantee correct behavior.

------------------------------------------------------------

Liskov Substitution Principle

• Child object should safely replace parent object.
• Focuses on Behavior Preservation.
• Validates whether inheritance is appropriate.
• Guarantees Runtime Polymorphism behaves correctly.

Memory Trick

Inheritance

↓

Code Reuse

--------------------------------

LSP

↓

Behavior Preservation

--------------------------------

Every LSP uses Inheritance.

BUT

Not every Inheritance follows LSP.

